    DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

    Header values that are lists or non-string values must be sent over HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 as they are over
    HTTP/1.1: one field per list element, and scalar values formatted as text.  Repeated response headers such
    as Set-Cookie must never be dropped or combined.

    Header names are case-insensitive: a handler header with a non-canonical name must replace the server's own
    field of the same name, never be sent together with it.
